@page "/help"
@inject NavigationManager Nav

@*
    Help — short, friendly, written in Bell's voice. No FAQ wall, no
    accordion. The page is the help. Headings double as anchors so
    every other surface can link straight to a section.
*@

<div class="page help-page">
    <header class="page-head">
        <div class="help-bell">
            <Bell State="cheering" />
        </div>
        <h1 class="page-title">A quick tour with Bell</h1>
        <p class="page-sub">Three minutes. By the end you'll know everything Bell can do.</p>
    </header>

    <section id="how-to-talk">
        <h2>1 · Three ways to talk to Bell</h2>
        <div class="help-cards">
            <article class="help-card">
                <h3>Tap and talk</h3>
                <p>The big blue <strong>Talk</strong> button on the home turns the mic on. Tap once, say what you'd like. Tap again to stop. Bell hears you, sends what you said, and shows the answer.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="help-card">
                <h3>Type</h3>
                <p>Tap the text field next to the mic and type. Bell handles short questions ("how do I boil an egg?") and long ones ("write me a letter to a landlord") the same way.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="help-card">
                <h3>Show</h3>
                <p>Tap the <strong>camera</strong> next to send to snap a picture and ask about it: a textbook page, a plant, a fridge, a recipe. Bell looks at it and answers.</p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section id="tiles">
        <h2>2 · The six starter tiles</h2>
        <p>Don't know where to begin? Tap one of the tiles on the home — Bell fills the box with a sensible question and waits for you to tweak it before sending.</p>
        <ul class="help-bullets">
            <li><strong>Help me write something.</strong> Emails, posts, letters, captions.</li>
            <li><strong>Help with homework.</strong> Maths, languages, history, science.</li>
            <li><strong>Tell me a story.</strong> Bedtime, school, just-for-fun.</li>
            <li><strong>Plan a meal.</strong> Tell Bell what's in the kitchen.</li>
            <li><strong>Make a picture.</strong> Bell draws what you describe.</li>
            <li><strong>Explain something.</strong> The why behind anything — at the level you ask for.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="menu">
        <h2>3 · The menu (the three dots)</h2>
        <p>Tap the three dots in the top-right and you'll find:</p>
        <ul class="help-bullets">
            <li><strong>New conversation</strong> — start a fresh chat.</li>
            <li><strong>History</strong> — every chat you've had, newest first.</li>
            <li><strong>Skills</strong> — specialists Bell can become for a chat.</li>
            <li><strong>Settings</strong> — voice, providers, theme, your API keys.</li>
            <li><strong>Switch mode</strong> — Grown-up, Kid, or Both.</li>
            <li><strong>Help</strong> — this page.</li>
            <li><strong>About</strong> — what Concierge is and who made it.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="privacy">
        <h2>4 · About privacy</h2>
        <p>Your chats live on your device. Bell only sends what you ask him to send. The mic only listens while the Talk button is highlighted. If you turn on Kid mode, recordings are never kept.</p>
        <p>Bell uses big AI providers (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, etc.) to think — your message goes to whichever you've connected and the answer comes back. Your API keys never leave your device.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="next">
        <h2>5 · What now?</h2>
        <div class="help-next">
            <a class="page-cta" href="/">Try a conversation</a>
            <a class="page-button quiet" href="/skills">Browse Bell's skills</a>
            <a class="page-button quiet" href="/settings">Connect a provider</a>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>
